  "evidence": [
    "Current producer62D5F0 writes id at allocated+4, name at+8, flags at+28 and advances40 bytes; receiver632DD0 consumes id/name/flags via existing NetPeerPlayerRecord with40-byte stride. Share this observed record, not a guessed class or new wire format.",
    "Preserve count low-byte-only publication, count*44+4 allocation despite40-byte records, source name truncation, all untouched header/name/tail bytes, sender flags/size/order and original allocation failure paths. No packet normalization or bounds fix.",
    "Group sender62F390 stores type word at+0 and sequence dword at+4 with eight-byte payload offset, already described by NetPacketEnvelope in receive owner. Use the same existing type, leave field2 and four-byte allocation tail untouched, keep reliable/retry behavior and historical obligations.",
    "Fresh before/after native whole-TU measurement, full application build/link, extracted owner and wire mutation controls, pinned layouts and independent review are required. No function-count promotion or acceptance claim."
  ],
  "intent": "Unify peer snapshot producer and receiver record ownership, and express group-send envelope fields through the existing wire type",
